  "prefLabel": "Bfa 102.02 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bfa 102.02 Purpose. In 1992 the general court continued, expanded, and modified the existing structure and powers of the industrial development authority, including renaming the agency the business finance authority. The purpose of the authority is to preserve, develop, and promote business and industry for the benefit of New Hampshire and its citizens. In order to meet its purpose, the authority interacts with business and industry.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Bfa 100) #5719, eff 10-13-93",
